docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:108:- Passwords are held only in memory in SQLAlchemy `URL` objects using the Psycopg driver. Configuration loading creates no engine or connection, logs nothing, and writes no credentials. Diagnostic representations exclude passwords; errors omit supplied values and underlying provider/parser exception details. Callers must not serialize passwords or render URLs with password hiding disabled in diagnostics.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:111:- Production is recognized but fails closed before reading local configuration or Windows credentials. Production identities and an independent secret provider require a separately approved deployment design; there is no reuse of local accounts or secret handling.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:132:`oaf_website/migration_authority.py` supplies the concrete file adapter and minimum deliberate issuer. The migration CLI consumes an existing authorization UUID; direct runner calls and Alembic enforce the same gate and run binding. Fixed environment claim slots prevent concurrent consumption even across different authorization IDs. All claims remain evidence, including partial writes. Completed issuance and terminal evidence use synchronized pending records and exclusive completion publication, bound to exact authorization/run UUIDs and evidence hashes; residual JSON alone never qualifies. Fully verified success, verified no-op, and conclusive safe premutation failure permit a new separately owner-authorized operation without exceptional reconciliation. Uncertain commits, postcommit audit failures, or incomplete/contradictory evidence require an explicit owner reconciliation attestation bound to the exact predecessor bytes and verified state. Development still requires completed successful testing validation of matching artifacts and its own authorization; reconciliation alone cannot supply that result. Exact authorization validity is rechecked after audit persistence immediately before mutation and commit. The migration connection explicitly requires `require_auth="scram-sha-256"`.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:275:State Request is **CLOSED / PASS**, and TESTING and DEVELOPMENT are at revision `0002_state_requests`, per the owner. This checkpoint authorizes notification source implementation and offline validation, superseding earlier notification deferral wording. It authorizes no live migrations, migration authorization issuance, credentials, email provider integration, production sending, separate administration system, or Git staging/commit/push. Preserve the F2 launcher, existing development environment, approved revisions 0001/0002 and owner-authored changes.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:277:- Keep the existing notification card and shared styling. Optional signup remains separate from anonymous State Requests; neither an account nor login is required. Choices are web launch, Android release, iOS release, and one of the 50 U.S. states for availability announcements. Selecting a state does not assert current availability or guarantee expansion.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:278:- Server eligibility requires a supported email address, at least one preference and explicit consent. Support common ASCII dot-atom email syntax with a DNS-style domain; trim outer ordinary spaces and lowercase the entire address for deduplication. Reject control characters, quoted/internationalized mailboxes and invalid/oversized inputs. Do not perform DNS requests or provider-specific dot/plus rewriting. Syntax validation does not verify mailbox ownership.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:280:- Revision `0003_notifications` follows unchanged 0002. The schema-qualified notification table stores normalized email, three launch preferences, optional state, fixed consent version, server consent timestamp, unsubscribe timestamp and a SHA-256 receipt hash. A partial unique email index permits at most one active subscription; the receipt-hash primary key prevents replay of a withdrawn lifecycle. Atomic conflict suppression preserves existing preferences, consent timestamps and tokens, including concurrent duplicates. Preference changes require the existing private unsubscribe link followed by fresh consent and a new receipt.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:284:- Email delivery is deferred. The UI confirms storage processing and explicitly states that no email has been sent; it never claims mailbox verification or a delivered confirmation. Future approved delivery must honor active consent/preferences and suppression, and establish mailbox verification and provider handling before dispatch. Announcement approval and geographic readiness remain Foundation decisions, with no AI runtime dependency.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:286:- Next database checkpoint: independent review of exact 0003 artifacts/prerequisites, then a separate owner-authorized **TESTING** `0002_state_requests -> 0003_notifications` validation. Verify real PostgreSQL partial-index races, constraints, dependency/type ACL and column-grant semantics, runtime identity, persistence, rollback/uncertain outcomes and real API/browser behavior. DEVELOPMENT requires successful TESTING evidence for matching artifacts and its own authorization. No live readiness is claimed by offline success.
