          <p class="eyebrow">Background &amp; Inspiration</p>
          <h2 id="story-title">Our Story</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="placeholder-text">The inspiration behind Ovis Alms Foundation can be traced to a familiar experience: wanting to help, yet finding the process more involved than it needed to be. Donating food, clothing, or household necessities often meant gathering items, arranging transportation, and delivering them to a charitable organization. Even with the best intentions, these efforts required considerable planning, while those receiving the goods had little choice in what was available.</p>
          <p class="placeholder-text">As shopping and financial transactions became possible through smartphones and computers, a new possibility emerged. Could someone enable another person to obtain daily necessities without the physical handoff while allowing that person greater freedom to choose what was most useful?</p>
          <p class="placeholder-text">But convenience was only part of the story. Personal encounters with people asking for money raised a deeper consideration. Faith encouraged an open heart rather than judgment, yet giving cash sometimes left an unanswered question: would it be spent on food or other necessities? Merchant eGift cards suggested a promising alternative&mdash;one that could preserve the spirit of compassion while offering recipients practical choices and directing charitable resources toward their intended purpose.</p>
          <p class="placeholder-text">Another question lingered long after a donation was made: Did my donation make a meaningful difference? A confirmation could show that the donation went through, but it could not tell the whole story of what became of it. Hearing firsthand from someone who had benefited&mdash;even through a simple, heartfelt expression of thanks&mdash;could transform that uncertainty into reassurance, satisfaction, and even renewed motivation to give again.</p>
          <p class="placeholder-text">Together, these experiences and reflections led to the establishment of Ovis Alms Foundation and the development of GraManna: an effort to fuse practical assistance and human appreciation into one continuing charitable experience.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
